{
  "version": 1,
  "_about": [
    "A demonstration pack built for a 30-minute walk around Belmont, Dayton OH.",
    "",
    "It exercises every feature of the engine: one spec theme using all of the",
    "mini-notation and every voice family, layers gated on all six mood",
    "dimensions, layer-level `when` conditions, and six cues covering all four",
    "ways of binding a loop to a place.",
    "",
    "The gate thresholds are tuned to this neighbourhood's ACTUAL measured mood",
    "range, surveyed at 17 points within 1 km:",
    "  energy     0.16 - 0.78     brightness 0.46 - 0.88",
    "  density    0.13 - 0.77     tension    0.08 - 0.22  <- narrow, see below",
    "  warmth     0.38 - 0.89     space      0.20 - 1.00",
    "",
    "Tension barely moves here — it is a calm residential area with no hospital",
    "or courthouse nearby. So the tension-gated layer uses a low threshold",
    "(0.13) instead of the 0.5 you would use in a city centre. Copying gate",
    "values from another neighbourhood is the most common reason a theme sounds",
    "dead: the layer never crosses its threshold.",
    "",
    "Cue thresholds are SHARES of the scene, measured at each anchor:",
    "  sacred 0.36 at the church vs 0.10-0.16 elsewhere",
    "  nature 0.39 at Belmont Park vs 0.06 elsewhere",
    "  sport  0.33 at the disc golf course, 0.35 at the gym, 0.00 elsewhere",
    "  nightlife 0.31 at the White Sail Inn, 0.00 elsewhere",
    "A dominant tag is around 0.2-0.4, never 1.0 — set thresholds accordingly.",
    ""
  ],
